---
import SoftwareLayout from '../../../layouts/SoftwareLayout.astro';
import data from '../../../../public/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/summary.json';
const base='/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/';
---
<SoftwareLayout title="Aero · Verification Bench" description="Real reference checks, measured failures, wall-treatment diagnostics and downloadable solver decks." canonicalPath="/software/aero/verification/" hideHeader>
  <div class="bench">
    <nav class="bench-nav" aria-label="Aero evidence navigation"><a href="/software/aero/#capability-papers">← Aero / See the evidence</a><a href="/software/aero/current/">Open workspace ↗</a></nav>
    <header class="bench-heading"><p class="eyebrow">VERIFICATION BENCH · REV 1.0</p><h1>A finished solve can still be wrong.</h1><p>Inspect the cases that pass, the controls that fail, and the evidence that tells them apart.</p><div class="actions"><a class="primary" href={base+'paper.pdf'}>Read the paper ↗</a><a href={base+'reproducibility.zip'} download>Download complete decks ↓</a></div></header>
    <nav class="case-nav" aria-label="Verification cases"><a href="#pipe">01 · Reference & failures</a><a href="#nozzle">02 · Wall treatment</a><a href="#cad">03 · Imperfect CAD</a><a href="#reproduce">04 · Reproduce</a></nav>
    <section id="pipe" aria-labelledby="pipe-title">
      <div class="section-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / LAMINAR PIPE · Re 200</p><h2 id="pipe-title">Same target. Five real outcomes.</h2></div><p>The analytical target is 0.64 Pa. Three grids pass the 2% allowance; two negative controls do not.</p></div>
      <figure><img src={base+'pipe-reference.png'} width="1728" height="608" alt="Pressure drop across five pipe cases, with the two negative controls outside the reference allowance; error decreases with grid refinement"/><figcaption>OpenFOAM Foundation 10 · fully developed circular-pipe flow · <a href={data.reference_url}>Poiseuille analytical reference</a>. Not an experimental validation.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Recorded pipe results — fixed reference and acceptance limits</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Case</th><th scope="col">Cells</th><th scope="col">Δp / Pa</th><th scope="col">Error</th><th scope="col">Gate</th></tr></thead><tbody>{data.pipe.map(r=><tr><th scope="row">{r.id.replace('pipe-','').replaceAll('-',' ')}</th><td>{r.cells.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{r.pressure_drop_pa.toFixed(6)}</td><td>{r.reference_error_pct.toFixed(3)}%</td><td><span class:list={['state',r.status==='ACCEPTED'?'pass':'fail']}>{r.status==='ACCEPTED'?'PASS':'FAIL'}</span></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <div class="case-inspector"><label for="pipe-choice">Inspect a gate</label><select id="pipe-choice" data-case-choice disabled>{data.pipe.map(r=><option value={r.id}>{r.id.replace('pipe-','')}</option>)}</select><p data-case-result role="status">All five recorded outcomes are shown in the table above. Interactive gate selection is available on the full bench page when JavaScript is enabled.</p><ul data-case-checks></ul></div>
      <div class="actions"><a href="/software/aero/current/?case=verification-pipe-fine-v1">Open passing case in Aero ↗</a><a href="/software/aero/current/?case=verification-pipe-underresolved-v1">Explore a failed case ↗</a></div>
      <details><summary>What was measured? What changed after the first diagnostic?</summary><p>D = 10 mm, L = 100 mm, bulk speed = 0.02 m/s, density = 1000 kg/m³, kinematic viscosity = 10⁻⁶ m²/s. Pressure is a fitted interior gradient × full length, not entrance loss. Darcy f = 64/Re = 0.32; Fanning f = 0.08.</p><p>The first gate rejected an ill-conditioned residual in an essentially zero transverse velocity. Criteria 1.1 introduced an explicit component-to-bulk scale check, then all seven CFD cases were rerun. This is a disclosed post-diagnostic correction, not a blind preregistration. Original diagnostic summaries remain in the archive. Pipe runs reached the fixed iteration limit; the explicit scale-aware acceptance checks are separate from the built-in stopping flag.</p><p>The underresolved case has two radial cells. The wrong-viscosity deck doubles viscosity without changing the original requirement. Their errors are measured, not assigned by a scripted FAIL label.</p></details>
      <h3>Conservation is a plot, not just a green cell.</h3><figure><img src={base+'conservation.png'} width="1728" height="608" loading="lazy" alt="Actual boundary flux imbalance versus SIMPLE iteration for the pipe and nozzle runs"/><figcaption>Actual inlet/outlet flux histories. Small imbalance does not guarantee reference agreement or convergence. Exact values are included as CSV; only the log plot clips values below 10⁻¹²%.</figcaption></figure>
    </section>
    <section id="nozzle" aria-labelledby="nozzle-title">
      <div class="section-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / NEW LOW-MACH NOZZLE DIAGNOSTIC</p><h2 id="nozzle-title">This mesh is not ready.</h2></div><span class="state fail">NOT ESTABLISHED</span></div>
      <p>Same 1,920-cell grid, same SST closure, different near-wall treatments. Both fail the selected y+ area screen. Their residual behavior differs; neither reaches the built-in stop. This does not revalidate the older wall-refinement-v6 case.</p>
      <figure><img src={base+'nozzle-yplus.png'} width="1728" height="608" loading="lazy" alt="Provisional nominal-area-weighted y plus histograms and axial values for wall-function and direct low-Re treatments"/><figcaption>Provisional diagnostics from the last solved fields, not validated wall-resolution evidence. Neither treatment meets its 95%-area criterion.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="metrics">{data.nozzle.map(r=><article><h3>{r.treatment==='low-re'?'Direct low-Re walls':'Wall-function treatment'}</h3><p>Maximum y+ <strong>{r.max_yplus.toFixed(2)}</strong></p><p>Area inside selected screen <strong>{(100*r.suitable_area_fraction).toFixed(1)}%</strong></p><span class="state fail">Near-wall screen FAIL</span><p>{r.treatment==='low-re'?'Active-field residuals are small; the negligible transverse component prevents the built-in stop.':'Significant active-field residuals remain at the iteration limit.'}</p></article>)}</div>
      <details><summary>Inspect residuals, thresholds and model assumptions</summary><figure><img src={base+'nozzle-residuals.png'} width="1728" height="608" loading="lazy" alt="All six nozzle residual histories, distinguishing the negligible transverse component from active-field residuals"/></figure><p>Bench screens: 95% of nominal wall area at 30 ≤ y+ ≤ 300 for the log-wall treatment; 95% at y+ ≤ 1 for direct low-Re walls. These are selected requirements, not universal validity laws. The two treatments may evaluate effective wall scaling differently; the comparison is not an independent wall-shear validation.</p><p>Direct low-Re pressure, in-plane velocity, k and omega residuals are below 10⁻¹⁰. Its normalized Uz residual remains about 0.003 despite max |Uz| / inlet speed being only 5.12 × 10⁻¹³. This is different from the wall-function case's significant active-field residuals. Both still fail near-wall suitability.</p><p>Inlet Re ≈ 5,333, no transition model, no independent nozzle reference. Direct-wall omega uses approximate first-cell height. The report explains what must be established before a performance prediction can be accepted.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section id="cad" aria-labelledby="cad-title">
      <div class="section-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / IMPORTED STEP · FILLET + INTERSECTING PORTS</p><h2 id="cad-title">Reject the defect. Keep the original.</h2></div><span class="state fail">SOLVER NOT SUBMITTED</span></div>
      <figure><img src={base+'cad-intake.png'} width="1728" height="688" loading="lazy" alt="Actual reimported manifold tessellations, with a red detached sliver in the rejected two-solid variant"/><figcaption>Synthetic fixtures exported and reimported through OpenCASCADE. The red sliver is 0.1 mm thick, shown at its real position. No silent repair.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="metrics"><article><h3>Intact manifold</h3><span class="state pass">Topology PASS</span><p>One valid connected solid. Physics, fluid region and boundary assignments remain missing: overall readiness is not established.</p></article><article><h3>Detached sliver</h3><span class="state fail">Intake FAIL</span><p>Two connected components violate the single-solid contract. Quarantined for review before mesh or solve. Multiple solids can be intentional elsewhere; this gate does not silently delete them.</p></article></div>
    </section>
    <section id="reproduce" aria-labelledby="reproduce-title"><p class="eyebrow">04 / VERSIONED, DOWNLOADABLE EVIDENCE</p><h2 id="reproduce-title">Keep the decks. Check the hashes.</h2><p>Seven new OpenFOAM runs, two STEP imports, and five retained CalculiX solves. {data.archive_file_count} hashed source and evidence files. These curated downloads have no 48-hour job expiration.</p><div class="actions"><a class="primary" href={base+'reproducibility.zip'} download>OpenFOAM + CalculiX decks ↓</a><a href={base+'paper.pdf'}>Paper PDF ↗</a><a href={base+'paper-sources.zip'} download>LaTeX + figures ↓</a><a href={base+'manifest.json'}>Public SHA-256 manifest</a></div><details><summary>Versions, reproduction commands and retained CalculiX scope</summary><p>OpenFOAM Foundation 10; CalculiX 2.20; Gmsh 4.15.2; CadQuery 2.7.0; OCP 7.8.1.1. The archive includes original decks, meshes, logs, final fields, criteria and an offline verifier. Local image IDs identify the executed environment; they are not public image download URLs.</p><pre>python source/audit.py .</pre><p>Run this after extracting the archive. Copy decks to a new scratch directory before rerunning. <a href={base+'README.md'}>Complete reproduction instructions</a> · <a href={base+'summary.json'}>Machine-readable results</a></p><p>The CalculiX subset contains the three-level pressure tube, a ported-tube fine solve and a thermal-gradient fine solve, recorded September 12. Original receipts preserve failed and incomplete gates. They are not five new solves.</p></details></section>
    <aside class="boundary"><h2>Engineering authority and limitations</h2><p>These deterministic checks demonstrate bounded numerical verification and rejection behavior—not experimental validation, general CAD robustness, autonomous LLM diagnosis, or design release. Hashes establish identity, not scientific validity. A source reference is not a local solve; an executed solve is not automatically an accepted prediction.</p></aside>
    <footer>Verification Bench Rev 1.0 · 13 September 2026 · Criteria 1.1, with disclosed post-diagnostic correction.<br/><a href="/software/aero/#capability-papers">Return to Aero evidence</a></footer>
  </div>
</SoftwareLayout>
<script>
import data from '../../../../public/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/summary.json';
const choice=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-case-choice]');
function inspect(){const r=data.pipe.find(x=>x.id===choice?.value);if(!r)return;const result=document.querySelector('[data-case-result]');if(result)result.textContent=`${r.status}: ${r.reference_error_pct.toFixed(3)}% reference error. ${r.failed_checks.length?'Failed checks: '+r.failed_checks.join(', '):'All six explicit acceptance checks pass.'}`;const list=document.querySelector('[data-case-checks]');if(list){list.replaceChildren(...Object.entries(r.checks).map(([k,v])=>{const li=document.createElement('li');li.textContent=`${v?'PASS':'FAIL'} · ${k.replaceAll('_',' ')}`;li.className=v?'pass':'fail';return li;}));}}
const requested=new URL(location.href).searchParams.get('case');if(choice){choice.disabled=false;if(data.pipe.some(r=>r.id===requested))choice.value=requested!;}
choice?.addEventListener('change',inspect);inspect();
</script>
<style>
.bench{max-width:1160px;margin:0 auto;padding:20px 24px 50px}.bench-nav,.actions,.case-nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;align-items:center}.bench-nav{justify-content:space-between;font-size:14px}.bench-heading{padding:38px 0 25px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.1em;font-weight:750;color:var(--accent)}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,55px);line-height:1.05;margin:12px 0}h2{font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,34px);line-height:1.15;margin:8px 0 16px}h3{font-size:20px}p{max-width:850px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)}.actions{margin:24px 0}.actions a{font-size:14px;font-weight:700}.primary{background:var(--accent);color:var(--bg);padding:12px 16px}.case-nav{border-block:1px solid var(--border);padding:15px 0;gap:12px 25px;font-size:14px}section{scroll-margin-top:20px;padding:36px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.section-title{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:25px}.section-title>p{max-width:380px}.state{display:inline-block;padding:6px 10px;border:1px solid currentColor;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;white-space:nowrap}.pass{color:#218063}.fail{color:#c54749}figure{margin:25px 0}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:white;border:1px solid var(--border)}figcaption{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;margin-top:10px}.table-wrap{overflow:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}caption{text-align:left;font-size:13px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--muted)}th,td{text-align:left;padding:12px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.case-inspector{padding:20px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);margin:22px 0}.case-inspector label{font-weight:700;margin-right:15px}select{padding:9px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--border);font:inherit;max-width:100%}.case-inspector ul{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 25px;font-size:13px;padding-left:20px}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.metrics article{padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface)}details{padding:16px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650;color:var(--text)}pre{overflow:auto;padding:15px;background:var(--surface)}.boundary{padding:28px 0}.boundary h2{font-size:20px}footer{font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted);border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:20px}@media(max-width:720px){.bench{padding:14px 16px}.section-title{display:block}.metrics{grid-template-columns:1fr}.section-title>p{max-width:none}.case-nav{gap:12px}th,td{padding:9px 7px}}
</style>
